# STORY-009 / ADR-003: runtime settings for `docker compose` (local runs only; Jenkins uses its own credential).
# One-time setup: copy this file to .env next to docker-compose.yml and put a password after DB_PASSWORD=.
# .env is git-ignored: never commit it, and never put a value in this file.
#
# DB_PASSWORD  Password of the PostgreSQL role ivirma_app. The db container sets it when the database volume
#              is first created; the backend connects with it. Any strong value, for example the output of
#              `openssl rand -hex 24`. Changing it later needs `docker compose down -v` (deletes the data).
DB_PASSWORD=
